cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its feature definitions, please cite it as below."
title: "interactional-features-ja: quantifying interactional features of Japanese everyday conversation"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible pipeline for measuring 19 interactional features (speech timing,
  fillers, sequence organisation, response types) from Japanese everyday
  conversation, together with the validation analyses reported in the
  accompanying manuscript. All five trait dimensions are analysed at equal
  granularity: Ridge regression over the 19 features plus speaker sex and age,
  under a subject-wise GroupKFold split, permutation tests with Holm correction,
  coefficient-level permutation tests combined with bootstrap stability, a
  disclosure of how many features each decision rule identifies,
  sensitivity analyses over preprocessing, regularisation strength and
  cross-validation choices, an a priori estimate of the effect size the design can
  detect, and baseline conditions that test whether the language-model scores depend
  on the transcript content. Correlation, coefficient of determination and RMSE are
  reported together, since ridge shrinkage makes a correlation alone a weak
  summary of fit. A synthetic dataset built from published summary statistics only
  is included so that the pipeline can be run without the corpus; it does not
  reproduce the reported results.
